text:
Styling and layout
The site uses Quarto’s default theme in light mode and darkly in dark mode. theme: picks others from Quarto’s built-in themes (the Bootswatch themes, as in pkgdown’s template: bootswatch:), with quartodown’s styling on top:
theme:
  light: flatly
  dark: darkly
Either can be left out to keep its default. A theme can also be your own .scss file in _quartodown/, such as light: _quartodown/brand.scss. To adjust a built-in theme you can use extra.scss, an example is given below.






TipA crowded navbar





Some themes space the navbar’s items further apart or capitalize them. With lux, for example, “Get started” wraps onto two lines and the version is cut off. Bringing the items closer in _quartodown/extra.scss fixes it:
/*-- scss:rules --*/
.navbar .nav-item {
  margin-right: 0.25rem;
}

.navbar .nav-link,
.navbar-brand {
  white-space: nowrap;
}



To restyle every page, add _quartodown/extra.scss. It is compiled on top of quartodown’s theme, once for the light theme and once for the dark one, and has two parts: Bootstrap and Quarto variables under scss:defaults, and CSS rules under scss:rules:
/*-- scss:defaults --*/
1$primary: #2c7a7b;
$font-family-sans-serif: "Inter", sans-serif;

/*-- scss:rules --*/
.navbar {
2  border-bottom: 1px solid $border-color;
}

1

Links, the active navbar item and buttons.

2

Variables take the value of the theme being compiled, so this suits both.


Plain CSS can go in _quartodown/extra.css instead, which is added to every page as it is.
The page’s widths and spacing are Quarto settings, under quarto:. For example, a wider text column and table of contents:
quarto:
  format:
    html:
      grid:
        body-width: 900px
        margin-width: 300px
See Quarto’s page layout guide for grid: and page-layout:.
The navbar’s items start where the page’s text does, which a script on each page measures. To start them at the edge of the page instead, override it with:
/*-- scss:rules --*/
.navbar-container {
  padding-left: 1em !important;
}
Everything in _quartodown/ is copied into the Quarto project, so other files it holds can be named from quarto: by the same path, such as Quarto template partials:
quarto:
  format:
    html:
      template-partials:
        - _quartodown/title-block.html
Setting include-in-header: or include-after-body: replaces quartodown’s own files, which, among other things, pick dark mode for visitors who prefer it and line up the navbar. To add to them, list them too:
quarto:
  format:
    html:
      include-in-header:
        - quartodown-header.html
        - _quartodown/analytics.html

Every page, help pages included, is a Quarto page, so you get:

every Quarto feature, from callouts and tabsets to code annotations and cross-references, on every page;
Quarto’s themes, extensions and settings.

On top of that, quartodown adds:

the package website layout R users know from pkgdown: a home page sidebar, a grouped function reference, articles and a changelog;
function links with hover tooltips.

A custom look
_quartodown/extra.scss restyles any part of the site, on top of the theme: here a navbar in the accent color, serif headings, rounder code blocks and the function reference as cards.








NoteThe settings





_quartodown/extra.scss:
/*-- scss:defaults --*/
// A teal accent and serif headings, in both themes.
$primary: #0f766e;
$headings-font-family: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;

/*-- scss:rules --*/
// The navbar as a band of the accent color, with light text and icons.
.navbar {
  background-color: $primary !important;
  --bs-navbar-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85) !important;
  --bs-navbar-hover-color: #fff !important;
  --bs-navbar-active-color: #fff !important;
  --bs-navbar-brand-color: #fff !important;
  --bs-navbar-brand-hover-color: #fff !important;
}

.navbar-title {
  font-family: $headings-font-family;
}

.navbar-nav .nav-link:hover,
.navbar .quarto-navigation-tool:hover {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15) !important;
}

.navbar-nav .nav-link.active {
  border-bottom-color: #fff;
}

.navbar .quarto-navigation-tool {
  color: #fff !important;
}

.navbar .quarto-color-scheme-toggle .bi::before {
  filter: brightness(0) invert(1);
}

// Rounder code blocks, marked with the accent.
div.sourceCode {
  border-radius: 0.75rem;
  border-left: 4px solid $primary;
}

// Each function on the reference index as a card.
dl.ref-index dt,
dl.ref-index dd {
  background: rgba($body-color, 0.04);
  border: 1px solid rgba($body-color, 0.1);
  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
}

dl.ref-index dt {
  border-bottom: none;
  border-radius: 0.75rem 0.75rem 0 0;
}

dl.ref-index dd {
  border-top: none;
  border-radius: 0 0 0.75rem 0.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
